note SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
note capprobe.om: does this omc admit a 55888-byte devcall (the utilization control's params)?
note Issues the NV_ESC_RM_CONTROL request 3223340586 on /dev/null, which is not a GPU device:
note the kernel answers ENOTTY (-25) when the call is made. An omc without the aien-dev/omega-mv#1042
note bound traps 3 at the devcall instead (exit 103). Exit 0: the call was made and returned -25.
text cpnull "/dev/null"
global cphdr uchar 32
global cpbuf uchar 55888

fn main to int
fd = fopen cpnull 0 len cpnull 524290 0
if lt fd 0
ret 1
end
r = devcall int fd uint 3223340586 cphdr 0 32 cpbuf 0 55888
c = fclose int fd
if ne r -25
ret 2
end
ret 0
end
